WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
We built a simulator where a robot arm has to cut hair.

00:04.000 --> 00:06.240
The hair starts at different lengths.

00:06.240 --> 00:08.840
The goal is to get it close to the same length

00:08.840 --> 00:10.720
without touching the scalp.

00:10.720 --> 00:14.000
The agent sees two cameras, one outside the head

00:14.000 --> 00:15.440
and one on the arm.

00:15.440 --> 00:17.840
It also gets the position of the blade.

00:17.840 --> 00:21.960
It can turn one joint, move the outside camera, or cut.

00:21.960 --> 00:24.760
It gets 252 moves.

00:24.760 --> 00:28.080
If the blade is too far away, nothing gets cut.

00:28.080 --> 00:30.240
This is an early run with Terra.

00:30.240 --> 00:34.440
It nicked the scalp 66 times, all while moving the arm.

00:34.440 --> 00:37.780
We moved the blade camera back, fixed how the hair was drawn,

00:37.780 --> 00:39.720
and added smaller turns.

00:39.720 --> 00:43.400
We ran Terra twice with those changes and Luna once.

00:43.400 --> 00:45.640
Both Terra runs had no nicks.

00:45.640 --> 00:47.240
Luna had two.

00:47.240 --> 00:49.880
In each run, at most one patch of hair

00:49.880 --> 00:51.640
ended up at the right length.

00:51.640 --> 00:54.200
We wrote a controller that uses the same moves

00:54.200 --> 00:55.520
and blade position.

00:55.520 --> 00:58.160
It knows the shape of the arm, where it starts,

00:58.160 --> 01:00.040
and the usual shape of the head.

01:00.040 --> 01:03.320
It got 16 of 42 patches to the right length

01:03.320 --> 01:06.200
on the same head without any nicks.

01:06.200 --> 01:08.600
Here is a separate run with the mohawk.

01:08.600 --> 01:11.880
The scripted controller in this run gets depth readings.

01:11.880 --> 01:14.680
It trimmed all 16 patches in the middle.

01:14.680 --> 01:17.871
10 ended up at the right length and there were no nicks.
